# KABU DIGITALS

KABU DIGITALS is a static website with an Express backend and SQLite lead dashboard.

## Deploy on Render

Deploy the repository with **New -> Blueprint**. Render uses the root `render.yaml`.

The single web service serves both the public website and the API:

- Website: `https://your-service.onrender.com/`
- Health check: `https://your-service.onrender.com/api/health`
- Admin login: `https://your-service.onrender.com/admin/login.html`

During Blueprint setup, provide `ADMIN_EMAIL`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`, and `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. Set `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to the exact Render service URL, including `https://`. `JWT_SECRET` is generated automatically. The blueprint uses a persistent disk for SQLite, so it uses Render's Starter plan.

## Local development

```powershell
npm install
$env:JWT_SECRET='local-development-secret'
$env:ADMIN_EMAIL='admin@example.com'
$env:ADMIN_PASSWORD='change-this-password'
npm start
```

Open `http://localhost:4000/` for the website or `http://localhost:4000/admin/login.html` for the dashboard.

## Project layout

- `frontend/` - public HTML, CSS, and JavaScript
- `backend/` - Express API, admin UI, and SQLite database access
- `render.yaml` - the only deployment blueprint

The contact form posts to the same origin in production. If the API is unavailable, it opens a pre-filled email fallback. Keep `.env` and database files out of version control.
